cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below
  (the archived Zenodo release of the version you used). If you use the
  salmon atlas, also cite Marco A. Vindas as its author; if you use the
  zebrafish atlas, also cite Wullimann, Rupp & Reichert (1996).
type: software
title: The Great IHC Leap Forward
abstract: >-
  A desktop app and pipeline for blinded, atlas-guided quantification of
  immunofluorescence in whole-brain sections of fish, from Zeiss CZI
  whole-slide scans to per-region cell densities. It builds contact sheets
  and QC for every section, lets an operator assign atlas plates and draw
  anatomical regions in a browser-based curator, maps those regions back to
  the native-resolution scan, segments nuclei with StarDist and measures each
  marker inside them. Salmon (Vindas) and zebrafish (Wullimann 1996) atlases
  ship ready to use, and custom atlases can be imported from Fiji ROIs.
